---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { t } from "../i18n";

const locale = "en";
const title = `${t("site.name", locale)} · The story`;
const description =
  "From a 610-metre grass strip in 1978 and a £85 ticket on Christmas Eve 1985 to the world's most scenic approach and Ireland's first ACA Level 4 carbon-accredited airport. The story of CFN.";

// 6 chapters, presented as horizontal panels on desktop (sticky
// horizontal scroll cabled in animations.ts via [data-horizontal])
// and as a vertical stack on mobile. Each panel carries the year as
// the dominant visual element. The text columns are intentionally
// narrow within the panel so the year breathes.
const chapters = [
  {
    year: "1978",
    range: "Before the airport",
    title: "A grass strip on the dunes.",
    lead:
      "The IDA needed an air link for the new industrial estate at Annagry. In March 1978, on a sandbar between the Atlantic and Mount Errigal, a 610-metre grass runway opened.",
    body: [
      "For seven years no scheduled flight took off from it. A handful of private aircraft, the odd connection to Derry, and a runway that disappeared under blown sand every winter.",
      "By the mid-1980s the grass was replaced with a hard surface and a temporary prefab terminal went up. Donegal had an aerodrome. It just didn't have an airline yet.",
    ],
  },
  {
    year: "1985",
    range: "Christmas Eve",
    title: "A lawyer, an Islander, an eighty-five-pound ticket.",
    lead:
      "On Christmas Eve 1985 Frank Cannon — a Glasgow solicitor with a father from Ardara and a mother from Ranafast — flew the first commercial service himself. A nine-seat Britten-Norman Islander, fifty-five minutes to Glasgow, £85 one way.",
    body: [
      "The idea had been hatched over dinner with Danny \"Minnie\" O'Brien in Annagry. The airline was Malinair. By the summer of 1986 it was running ten rotations a day from six in the morning, the Islanders had been replaced by Dorniers, and Edinburgh and Manchester were on the timetable.",
      "By 1987 Malinair was bankrupt and Air Ecosse stepped in for a few weeks. The airline went under. The airport carried on.",
    ],
  },
  {
    year: "1988",
    range: "The Loganair years",
    title: "Loganair returns. Ryanair tries Luton.",
    lead:
      "In 1988 Loganair came back with a regular service to Glasgow and stayed for a decade. The runway was extended at the end of the eighties to 1,450 metres, and again in 1992–93 to 1,500 metres. In 1990 Ryanair launched a service to London Luton.",
    body: [
      "In the winter of 1994 a storm ran for weeks. The ferry to Tory Island couldn't sail. The Irish Air Corps moved their helicopters to Carrickfinn and ran supplies — bread, post, prescriptions, schoolchildren — out to the island until the sea calmed down. The pattern stuck: for decades after, the helicopter to Tory would route through CFN whenever the weather closed in on Magheroarty.",
    ],
  },
  {
    year: "1996",
    range: "The PSO years",
    title: "Dublin every day.",
    lead:
      "In August 1996 the Donegal–Dublin PSO was awarded for the first time, one of the very first PSO routes in Ireland.",
    body: [
      "Ireland Airways flew it, then Aer Arann from 1998, then Euroceltic, then Aer Arann again. By 2008 the airport was carrying 65,539 passengers — the all-time record.",
    ],
  },
  {
    year: "2001",
    range: "Helicopters out west",
    title: "The Atlantic margin runs on Donegal fuel.",
    lead:
      "For a stretch of about a decade Donegal was something else entirely: the closest paved runway with refuelling to the offshore oil and gas exploration in the Atlantic margin. Bristow Helicopters ran the shuttle.",
    body: [
      "Two basins drove the traffic. The Slyne-Erris Trough off Mayo, where the Corrib gas field had been discovered in 1996, and the deeper Rockall Trough where in 2002 Enterprise drilled the Dooish well — 125 kilometres northwest of Donegal, 1,478 metres of water under the rig. Both campaigns needed crews changed every couple of weeks and a fuel stop that wasn't four hundred miles away.",
    ],
  },
  {
    year: "2025",
    range: "Today",
    title: "Greener than Dublin.",
    lead:
      "In January 2025 Donegal became the first airport on the island of Ireland to reach Airport Carbon Accreditation Level 4 \"Transformation\" — ahead of Dublin, Cork and Shannon.",
    body: [
      "Solar on the hangar roof. MVHR through the terminal. LED everything. Four 22-kilowatt EV chargers in the car park. The road to a seventy-per-cent reduction in scope-1 and scope-2 emissions by 2030, and Net Zero by 2050.",
      "Emerald Airlines flies Dublin twice a day under the Aer Lingus Regional brand. Loganair is year-round to Glasgow. The airport carried 50,530 passengers in 2024, up twenty-one per cent.",
    ],
  },
];

const airlines = [
  { name: "Malinair", route: "Glasgow / Manchester / Edinburgh", years: "1985 – 1987" },
  { name: "Air Ecosse", route: "Glasgow", years: "1987" },
  { name: "Loganair", route: "Glasgow", years: "1988 – 1997" },
  { name: "Ryanair", route: "London Luton", years: "from 1990" },
  { name: "Macair", route: "—", years: "1995" },
  { name: "Gill Airways", route: "Glasgow Prestwick", years: "1996 –" },
  { name: "Ireland Airways", route: "Dublin PSO", years: "1996 – 1998" },
  { name: "Bright Air", route: "Glasgow", years: "1997/98 –" },
  { name: "Aer Arann", route: "Dublin · Cork · Glasgow Intl.", years: "1998 – 2015" },
  { name: "Euroceltic", route: "Dublin PSO", years: "2001 – 2003" },
  { name: "Loganair / Flybe", route: "Dublin", years: "2012 – 2015" },
  { name: "Stobart Air (Aer Lingus Regional)", route: "Dublin PSO", years: "2015 – 2021" },
  { name: "Amapola Flyg", route: "Dublin PSO (interim)", years: "2021 – 2022" },
  { name: "Emerald Airlines (Aer Lingus Regional)", route: "Dublin PSO · 2× daily", years: "2022 – today" },
  { name: "Loganair (relaunch)", route: "Glasgow · year-round", years: "2023 – today" },
] as const;
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  {/* ---------- HERO — text only, kept short ---------- */}
  <section
    class="relative isolate flex min-h-[72vh] w-full items-end border-b border-line bg-surface-lo/40"
  >
    <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-7xl px-6 pb-16 pt-40 sm:pb-24">
      <p
        data-animate="fade-up"
        class="font-mono text-[0.7rem] uppercase tracking-[0.32em] text-atlantic"
      >
        About · An scéal
      </p>
      <h1
        data-split
        data-split-delay="0.1"
        class="mt-8 max-w-5xl font-display text-[clamp(2.75rem,7vw,7.5rem)] font-light leading-[0.95] text-ink"
      >
        Forty years on the beach.
      </h1>
      <p
        data-animate="fade-up"
        data-animate-delay="0.35"
        class="mt-10 max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-mute sm:text-lg"
      >
        Six chapters · 1978 to 2025. Scroll right to travel
        forward through the airport's life.
      </p>

      <div
        data-animate="fade-up"
        data-animate-delay="0.5"
        class="mt-12 flex items-center gap-3 text-mute"
        aria-hidden="true"
      >
        <span class="scroll-hint font-mono text-[0.65rem] uppercase tracking-[0.24em]">
          Scroll
        </span>
        <span class="scroll-hint text-base">→</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ---------- HORIZONTAL TIMELINE — desktop only ----------
       The wrapper is tall (one viewport per panel of vertical
       scroll distance). h-pin sticks to viewport; h-track
       translates -X as the user scrolls down. animations.ts wires
       this up via [data-horizontal]. */}
  <section
    data-horizontal
    class="h-wrapper relative hidden bg-surface lg:block"
    style={`height: ${(chapters.length + 0.5) * 100}vh;`}
  >
    <div class="h-pin">
      {/* Floating progress strip — dots with year labels */}
      <nav
        aria-label="Chapter progress"
        class="absolute left-1/2 top-10 z-20 -translate-x-1/2"
      >
        <ol
          data-h-progress
          class="flex items-center gap-5 rounded-full border border-line/80 bg-surface-hi/85 px-5 py-2.5 font-mono text-[0.66rem] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-mute shadow-[0_8px_24px_-18px_rgba(17,32,45,0.25)] backdrop-blur"
        >
          {
            chapters.map((c, i) => (
              <li>
                <a
                  href={`#chapter-${i}`}
                  data-h-dot
                  data-index={i}
                  class="group inline-flex items-center gap-2 transition-colors hover:text-atlantic"
                >
                  <span
                    class="inline-block h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-mute transition-all duration-300 group-hover:bg-atlantic"
                  />
                  <span class="tabular-nums">{c.year}</span>
                </a>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ol>
      </nav>

      {/* The horizontal track of chapter panels */}
      <div class="h-track items-stretch py-12">
        {/* Intro panel — eyebrow / instructions */}
        <article
          class="flex h-[calc(100vh-6rem)] w-[40rem] shrink-0 flex-col justify-center pl-[clamp(1.5rem,6vw,6rem)] pr-12"
        >
          <p class="font-mono text-[0.7rem] uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-atlantic">
            The timeline
          </p>
          <h2
            class="mt-5 max-w-md font-display text-[clamp(2.5rem,4.5vw,4.5rem)] font-light leading-[1]"
          >
            Six chapters, one runway.
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-7 max-w-sm text-base leading-relaxed text-mute">
            From a grass strip with no airline in 1978 to Ireland's
            greenest small airport in 2025. The story moves to the
            right — like the runway itself.
          </p>
          <p
            class="mt-10 inline-flex items-center gap-3 font-mono text-[0.65rem] uppercase tracking-[0.24em] text-sand"
            aria-hidden="true"
          >
            <span>Scroll to begin</span>
            <span class="text-base">→</span>
          </p>
        </article>

        {/* The six story panels */}
        {
          chapters.map((c, i) => (
            <article
              id={`chapter-${i}`}
              data-h-panel
              data-index={i}
              class="relative flex h-[calc(100vh-6rem)] w-[58rem] shrink-0 items-stretch"
            >
              {/* Big year as architectural background */}
              <span
                aria-hidden="true"
                class="pointer-events-none absolute -left-4 top-1/2 -z-10 -translate-y-1/2 select-none font-display font-light leading-none text-sand/15"
                style="font-size: clamp(12rem, 32vh, 28rem);"
              >
                {c.year}
              </span>

              {/* Text column */}
              <div class="relative z-10 flex w-full flex-col justify-center pl-[clamp(2rem,6vw,8rem)] pr-12">
                <p
                  data-animate="fade-up"
                  class="font-mono text-[0.72rem] uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-sand"
                >
                  <span>{`0${i + 1}`.slice(-2)} · {c.range}</span>
                  <span class="ml-3 text-atlantic">{c.year}</span>
                </p>

                <h2
                  data-split
                  class="mt-5 max-w-2xl font-display text-[clamp(2rem,4vw,4rem)] font-light leading-[1.02] text-ink"
                >
                  {c.title}
                </h2>

                <p
                  data-animate="fade-up"
                  data-animate-delay="0.18"
                  class="mt-7 max-w-xl text-[1.05rem] leading-[1.7] text-ink sm:text-[1.12rem]"
                >
                  {c.lead}
                </p>

                {c.body.map((para, j) => (
                  <p
                    data-animate="fade-up"
                    data-animate-delay={`${0.25 + j * 0.06}`}
                    class="mt-5 max-w-xl text-base leading-[1.7] text-mute"
                  >
                    {para}
                  </p>
                ))}
              </div>
            </article>
          ))
        }

        {/* Outro panel — handoff to the operators table */}
        <article
          class="flex h-[calc(100vh-6rem)] w-[32rem] shrink-0 flex-col justify-center px-12"
        >
          <p class="font-mono text-[0.7rem] uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-atlantic">
            Continues below
          </p>
          <h2
            class="mt-4 max-w-md font-display text-[clamp(2rem,3.6vw,3.4rem)] font-light leading-[1]"
          >
            Every airline that has ever flown here.
          </h2>
          <p
            class="mt-8 inline-flex items-center gap-3 font-mono text-[0.65rem] uppercase tracking-[0.24em] text-sand"
            aria-hidden="true"
          >
            <span>Scroll down</span>
            <span class="text-base">↓</span>
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ---------- VERTICAL TIMELINE — mobile fallback ---------- */}
  <section class="border-y border-line lg:hidden">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-6 py-20">
      <ol class="space-y-20">
        {
          chapters.map((c, i) => (
            <li class="relative">
              <span
                aria-hidden="true"
                class="pointer-events-none absolute -left-2 -top-6 -z-10 select-none font-display text-7xl font-light leading-none text-sand/20"
              >
                {c.year}
              </span>
              <p
                data-animate="fade-up"
                class="font-mono text-[0.7rem] uppercase tracking-[0.28em] text-sand"
              >
                {`0${i + 1}`.slice(-2)} · {c.range}{" "}
                <span class="text-atlantic">{c.year}</span>
              </p>
              <h2
                data-split
                class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl font-light leading-[1.05] text-ink"
              >
                {c.title}
              </h2>
              <p class="mt-5 text-[1.05rem] leading-[1.65] text-ink">
                {c.lead}
              </p>
              {c.body.map((para) => (
                <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-[1.7] text-mute">{para}</p>
              ))}
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ---------- AIRLINES TABLE ---------- */}
  <section class="border-t border-line bg-surface-lo/60">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-24">
      <p
        data-animate="fade-up"
        class="font-mono text-[0.7rem] uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-atlantic"
      >
        Operators
      </p>
      <h2
        data-split
        class="mt-3 max-w-3xl font-display text-[clamp(2rem,4vw,3.4rem)] font-light leading-[1.04]"
      >
        Every airline that has flown to Donegal.
      </h2>

      <div data-animate="fade-up" class="mt-12 overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="w-full min-w-[560px] border-collapse text-left">
          <thead>
            <tr class="border-y border-line text-[0.66rem] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-mute">
              <th class="py-3 pr-6 font-medium">Airline</th>
              <th class="py-3 pr-6 font-medium">Route</th>
              <th class="py-3 font-medium">Years</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="font-mono text-sm">
            {
              airlines.map((a) => (
                <tr class="border-b border-line/60">
                  <td class="py-4 pr-6 text-ink">{a.name}</td>
                  <td class="py-4 pr-6 text-mute">{a.route}</td>
                  <td class="py-4 tabular-nums text-mute">{a.years}</td>
                </tr>
              ))
            }
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
